a. provide education about education, ideology, and nationalism values;
b. provide counseling about the dangers of terrorism;
c. provide social rehabilitation; and
d. provide social assistance.

Article 32
Education as referred to in article 31 is directed towards:
a. the development of the child's personality, talents, mental and physical abilities to their fullest potential;
b. the development of respect for human rights and fundamental freedoms;
c. the development of respect for the child's parents, cultural identity, language, and values, the national values of the country in which the child is living, the country from which the child may originate, and the diverse customs of the child's own place of residence;
d. the preparation of the child for a responsible life; and
e. the development of respect and love for the environment.

Article 70
(1) Health recovery services as referred to in Article 66 paragraph (2) letter d number 1 include:
a. emergency services;
b. services for the provision of visum et repertum or visum psychiatricum in accordance with applicable provisions;
c. follow-up services in the form of outpatient and/or inpatient care in accordance with medical provisions;
d. deoxyribose nucleic acid verification services;
e. delivery process services for pregnancy as a result of sexual violence and/or rape;
f. services for providing further referrals in accordance with the circumstances and condition of the victim; and
g. services for providing special rooms separated from general patients.
(2) OPD responsible for health affairs is obligated to provide health recovery services.

